{"name":"Baby’s Blanket","hex":"#ffaec1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.\n\nA very young human, even if not yet born.","A very young human, even if not yet born."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"blanket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy, loosely woven fabric, usually large and woollen, used for warmth while sleeping or resting.","A covering layer of anything."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["General; covering or encompassing everything."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blanket"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of Crayola crayon colors","blocks":[{"text":"Since the introduction of Crayola drawing crayons by Binney & Smith in 1903, more than 200 colors have been produced in a wide variety of assortments. The table below represents all of the colors found in regular Crayola assortments from 1903 to the present. Since the introduction of fluorescent crayons in the 1970s, the standard colors have been complemented by a number of specialty crayon assortments, represented in subsequent tables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Crayola1.jpg/330px-Crayola1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Crayola_crayon_colors"},{"title":"Blanket","blocks":[{"text":"A blanket is a swath of smooth cloth large enough either to cover or to enfold most of the user's body and thick enough to keep the body warm by trapping radiant body heat that otherwise would be lost through convection and radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Lautrec_in_bed_1893.jpg/330px-Lautrec_in_bed_1893.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blanket"},{"title":"Infant","blocks":[{"text":"An infant is a very young human being. Baby is an alternative term for infant. The terms may also be used to refer to juvenile beings of other organisms. A newborn is, in mainstream use, an infant who is only hours, days, or weeks old; while in medical contexts, a newborn or neonate is an infant in the first 28 days after birth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg/330px-The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infant"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Silverswirlss.png/500px-Silverswirlss.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Silverswirlss.png/1280px-Silverswirlss.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Silverswirlss.png/500px-Silverswirlss.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"16 of the 24 Silver Swirls colors","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilverswirlss.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Crayonscent.png/330px-Crayonscent.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Crayonscent.png/330px-Crayonscent.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"16 of the 30 Crayola Magic Scent Crayons (showing Leather Jacket, Dirt, Fresh Air, Eucalyptus, Baby Powder, Shampoo, Rose, Daffodil, Smoke, Lumber, Cedar Chest, Lilac, New Car, Tulip, Soap, and